  "_knownGaps": {
    "_": "Things published recipes ask for that this kitchen genuinely does not have, listed so the matcher reports them as MISSING with a real name rather than as UNKNOWN. Everything here has been hit by an actual rejected recipe.",
    "hondashi": "Japanese dashi powder, dried bonito and kelp. Rejected Aaron and Claire Ground Beef Gyudon on 2026-08-11. Chicken bouillon covers the salt but not the oceanic depth.",
    "kimchi": "Suggested alongside two Korean dishes, never required by one.",
    "gochujang": "Korean fermented chilli paste. Rejects most spicy Korean recipes.",
    "gochugaru": "Korean chilli flakes. Not the same as crushed red pepper: coarser, fruitier, much less hot.",
    "pancetta": "Rejected three separate frittata recipes on 2026-08-12. Bacon is the usual stand-in.",
    "tinned tomatoes": "Rejected the metric bolognese on 2026-08-11. NOTE: fresh grape tomatoes arrived 08-12, which changes what is possible but is still not the same product.",
    "kidney beans": "Blocks chilli con carne.",
    "enoki mushrooms": "Stringy, stays in strands. Cremini is meatier and not equivalent, though it works.",
    "wine": "No red or white wine in the kitchen. Blocks a lot of braises and many ragu recipes.",
    "heavy cream": "No cream. Milk is not a substitute in anything that reduces.",
    "sesame seeds": "Toasted sesame seeds, wanted as a garnish by most Korean recipes.",
    "pickled ginger": "Benishoga, garnish on gyudon. Marked optional by its own recipe.",
    "short grain rice": "Not owned. Long grain works but changes the dish: in a donburi the sauce is meant to soak a sticky layer of rice under the topping, and long grain stays separate so the sauce runs to the bottom of the bowl. About $5.77 and it unlocks every donburi plus the Beef Bulgogi pot rice already written."
  },
